{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 26, :comments ["<b>I call heaven and earth to witness against you this day.</b> The verse intended by this testimony of heaven and earth upon the angels and upon human beings. Or the intention is concerning the rain, to say: if they fulfill the Torah, it will rain, and if not, it will not rain, in the manner of what is written (Leviticus 26:19): ״ונתתי את שמיכם כברזל ואת ארצכם כנחשה״." "<b>And the sage</b> R. Abraham, of blessed memory, explained this: that he designated witnesses who would see them always — they and their children, generation after generation — for they stand eternal; and so (Micah 6): ״שמעו הרים את ריב ה׳״; and so (Joshua 24): ״הנה האבן הזאת תהיה בנו לעדה״."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 4, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:45:23.494312146Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}